      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks wrong.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times a day comes to **5,100 mg per day**. That's about twice the usual maximum for metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe stomach and bowel side effects, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\n**It may be one of these common orders:**\n- **Metformin 850 mg by mouth, three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n- **Metformin 1700 mg total per day**, given as 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- **Metformin 1000 mg by mouth, twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n\nPlease tell me which dose and frequency you meant, or confirm that you want 1700 mg three times daily on purpose. If you confirm, I'll enter it as written with a note about the over-maximum dose."
      }
     ],
